; 2026-09-06, real bug found while wiring in the stop-distance fix (user:
; "the eel just aligns its center to elana. but the attack zone is at one
; end of the eel. so nothing happens") -- this (32,0) offset was set on the
; CHILD CollisionShape2D here, but flying_enemy.gd's own direction-flip
; logic (_update_zones()) only ever repositions the AttackZone node ITSELF
; based on facing (reads $AttackZone.position.x once in _ready() as the
; offset magnitude, then re-signs it every frame) -- with the offset on the
; child instead, that read back 0, so the flip was a permanent no-op and
; the hitbox stayed pinned to a fixed world side regardless of which way
; the eel was actually facing/chasing. Moved up to AttackZone itself below.
[node name="AttackZone" parent="." index="4" unique_id=696568212]
position = Vector2(32, 0)

[node name="CollisionShape2D" parent="AttackZone" parent_id_path=PackedInt32Array(696568212) index="0" unique_id=476977613]
shape = SubResource("RectangleShape2D_eel_attack")

